@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `homecare-nouns`
IMPORT `homecare-definitions`
IMPORT `homecare-perils`
IMPORT `homecare-general-exclusions`
IMPORT `homecare-general-conditions`
IMPORT `homecare-part1`
IMPORT `homecare-test-fixtures`

-- Tests for the Definitions, the Insured Perils and Part 1. Every expected value was worked
-- out from the source text (the clause is cited beside each group) before the assertion was
-- run; none was copied from an evaluation. Policy Summary figures are the HYPOTHETICAL ones
-- of homecare-test-fixtures.l4. A failing assertion is a finding, never a value to edit.
--
-- For every exclusion there is a case that triggers it and a near miss that does not; where
-- the exclusion has a carve-back, the near miss is the carve-back.

§ `Tests: Definitions, Insured Perils, Part 1`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN loss IS A `A Part 1 loss`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground under Part 1`
`the grounds against` loss MEANS
    `the grounds on which a Part 1 claim fails, under` `the owner's policy` `with` `good conduct` `for` loss `, as at` `1 April 2026`

GIVEN loss IS A `A Part 1 loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`covered:` loss MEANS null (`the grounds against` loss)

GIVEN g    IS A `A ground under the Insured Perils`
      loss IS A `A Part 1 loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the peril ground` g `defeats` loss MEANS elem (`an Insured Peril ground` g) (`the grounds against` loss)

GIVEN g    IS A `A ground under Part 1`
      loss IS A `A Part 1 loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the ground` g `defeats` loss MEANS elem g (`the grounds against` loss)

-- The house damaged by fire with one circumstance.
GIVEN c IS A `A circumstance of a loss`
GIVETH A `A Part 1 loss`
`a house fire with` c MEANS `the house damaged by` `fire` `with` (LIST c)

§§ `Introduction: when cover attaches (src:21-24)`

GIVEN agreed  IS A BOOLEAN
      accepted IS A BOOLEAN
      paid    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The policy`
`a policy where Certificate agreed` agreed `, proposal accepted` accepted `, premium paid in time` paid MEANS
    `The policy` WITH
        `the Policy Summary`                                     IS `the 2026 Summary`
        `the Insured`                                            IS `an Insured born 15 June 1980, a tenant` FALSE
        `the premises`                                           IS `a brick house`
        `issued to a company`                                    IS FALSE
        `the Insured also has Personal Accident cover`           IS FALSE
        `the Insurer agreed to issue a Certificate or the Policy Summary` IS agreed
        `the Insurer received and accepted a completed Proposal Form`     IS accepted
        `the premium was paid in full within the prescribed time`         IS paid
        `the premium paid`                                       IS 4_000_000

#ASSERT `cover has attached under` (`a policy where Certificate agreed` TRUE `, proposal accepted` FALSE `, premium paid in time` FALSE)
#ASSERT `cover has attached under` (`a policy where Certificate agreed` FALSE `, proposal accepted` TRUE `, premium paid in time` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `cover has attached under` (`a policy where Certificate agreed` FALSE `, proposal accepted` TRUE `, premium paid in time` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `cover has attached under` (`a policy where Certificate agreed` FALSE `, proposal accepted` FALSE `, premium paid in time` TRUE)
#ASSERT elem `Introduction: cover had not attached` (`the grounds on which a Part 1 claim fails, under` (`a policy where Certificate agreed` FALSE `, proposal accepted` TRUE `, premium paid in time` FALSE) `with` `good conduct` `for` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `, as at` `1 April 2026`)

§§ `The base case`

-- A house damaged by fire, nothing else ticked: covered, and nothing defeats it.
#ASSERT `the grounds against` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `covered:` (`a sofa damaged by` `fire` `with` EMPTY)

§§ `Period of Insurance (src:59-61, 402-404), fork F-period`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A Part 1 loss`
`a house fire on` d MEANS
    `a loss to` `the Home` `of` (LIST `the house or apartment itself`) `owned by` `the Insured` `at` `inside a lockable part of the Home`
        `on` d `by` `fire` `with` EMPTY `, unattended for` 0 `days`

-- The written claim is delivered five days after each loss, so GC4(g) is met.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground under Part 1`
`the grounds against a house fire on` d MEANS
    `the grounds on which a Part 1 claim fails, under` `the owner's policy` `with` (`conduct with the written claim delivered` (JUST (d PLUS 5)))
        `for` (`a house fire on` d) `, as at` (d PLUS 10)

#ASSERT `the grounds against a house fire on` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the grounds against a house fire on` (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the grounds against a house fire on` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS (LIST `the loss was not in the Period of Insurance`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against a house fire on` (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS (LIST `the loss was not in the Period of Insurance`)

§§ `Insured Location and the Home as a building (src:69-80, 93-103), fork F-home-c`

GIVEN premises IS A `The insured premises`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a house fire is covered at` premises MEANS
    `Part 1 covers the loss, under` (`the owner's policy, at` premises) `with` `good conduct` `for` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `, as at` `1 April 2026`

#ASSERT `a house fire is covered at` (`premises that are a` `a house`)
#ASSERT `a house fire is covered at` (`premises that are a` `an apartment in an apartment building`)
#ASSERT NOT `a house fire is covered at` (`premises that are a` `a hotel`)
#ASSERT NOT `a house fire is covered at` (`premises that are a` `a boarding house`)
#ASSERT NOT `a house fire is covered at` (`premises that are a` `a strata-title apartment`)
#ASSERT NOT `a house fire is covered at` (`premises that are a` `a mobile home`)
#ASSERT NOT `a house fire is covered at` (`premises that are a` `another kind of building`)

-- The construction requirement, and the Summary's special provision that lifts it.
GIVEN `walls ok` IS A BOOLEAN
      `roof ok`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The insured premises`
`a house with walls ok` `walls ok` `, roof ok` `roof ok` MEANS
    `The insured premises` WITH
        `the kind of building`                                     IS `a house`
        `at the address in the Policy Summary`                     IS TRUE
        `the Insured's principal personal residence`               IS TRUE
        `used wholly or mainly as the Insured's private residence` IS TRUE
        `part used as an office`                                   IS FALSE
        `office use approved by the authorities`                   IS FALSE
        `used for a trade or business other than an office`        IS FALSE
        `walls of concrete, brick or stone`                        IS `walls ok`
        `roof of concrete, tiles, slate or incombustible metal sheet` IS `roof ok`
        `under construction`                                       IS FALSE
        `being demolished or vacant pending demolition`            IS FALSE
        `a temporary building or structure`                        IS FALSE
        `enclosed by walls or fences`                              IS TRUE
        `some part is lent, let or sublet`                         IS FALSE
        `some part is used to manufacture, deposit or store goods` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `a house fire is covered at` (`a house with walls ok` TRUE `, roof ok` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a house fire is covered at` (`a house with walls ok` FALSE `, roof ok` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a house fire is covered at` (`a house with walls ok` TRUE `, roof ok` FALSE)

-- An office in part of the Home: covered only if the authorities approve.
GIVEN approved IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The insured premises`
`a house partly used as an office, approved` approved MEANS
    `The insured premises` WITH
        `the kind of building`                                     IS `a house`
        `at the address in the Policy Summary`                     IS TRUE
        `the Insured's principal personal residence`               IS TRUE
        `used wholly or mainly as the Insured's private residence` IS TRUE
        `part used as an office`                                   IS TRUE
        `office use approved by the authorities`                   IS approved
        `used for a trade or business other than an office`        IS FALSE
        `walls of concrete, brick or stone`                        IS TRUE
        `roof of concrete, tiles, slate or incombustible metal sheet` IS TRUE
        `under construction`                                       IS FALSE
        `being demolished or vacant pending demolition`            IS FALSE
        `a temporary building or structure`                        IS FALSE
        `enclosed by walls or fences`                              IS TRUE
        `some part is lent, let or sublet`                         IS FALSE
        `some part is used to manufacture, deposit or store goods` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `a house fire is covered at` (`a house partly used as an office, approved` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a house fire is covered at` (`a house partly used as an office, approved` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the premises are the Insured Location` (`a house partly used as an office, approved` FALSE)

