-- Near miss: the same act pleaded under limb (c), where it belongs.
#ASSERT `covered:` (`the house damaged by` `wilful act of a striker or locked-out worker` `with` (LIST `the act was intended to further a riot or strike or resist a lockout`))
#ASSERT `the peril ground` `Peril 4(i)(a): terrorism` `defeats` (`the house damaged by` `riot or civil disturbance` `with` (LIST `an act of terrorism`))
#ASSERT `the peril ground` `Peril 4(i)(b): civil commotion amounting to a popular rising` `defeats` (`the house damaged by` `riot or civil disturbance` `with` (LIST `civil commotion amounting to a popular rising`))
#ASSERT `the peril ground` `Peril 4(i)(c): wilful corruption of computer information` `defeats` (`the house damaged by` `malicious act of any person` `with` (LIST `wilful erasure, loss, distortion or corruption of computer information`))
#ASSERT `the peril ground` `Peril 4(ii)(a): consequential or indirect loss` `defeats` (`the house damaged by` `riot or civil disturbance` `with` (LIST `the loss claimed is consequential or indirect`))
#ASSERT `the peril ground` `Peril 4(ii)(b): cessation of work or interruption of a process` `defeats` (`the house damaged by` `wilful act of a striker or locked-out worker` `with` (LIST `cessation of work or interruption of a process or operation`))
#ASSERT `the peril ground` `Peril 4(ii)(c): confiscation, commandeering or requisition` `defeats` (`the house damaged by` `lawful authority suppressing a disturbance` `with` (LIST `dispossession by confiscation, commandeering or requisition`))
#ASSERT `the peril ground` `Peril 4(ii)(d): unlawful occupation of the Home` `defeats` (`the house damaged by` `riot or civil disturbance` `with` (LIST `dispossession of the Home by unlawful occupation`))
