§§ `Settlement: the basis, Provisions 1-3 (src:301-323)`

-- A Home loss of 300,000,000 to reinstate, Actual Value 200,000,000, Summary Deductible
-- 2,000,000 (hypothetical). Reinstated with dispatch and the cost incurred: 300,000,000 less
-- the Deductible = 298,000,000.
GIVEN f IS A `The figures for a Part 1 loss`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`a house fire, settled on` f MEANS
    `Part 1: the amount payable, under` `the owner's policy` `with` `good conduct` `for` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `on` f `, as at` `1 April 2026`

#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`figures: reinstatement` 300_000_000 `, Actual Value` 200_000_000 `, reinstated and incurred` TRUE `, cost if wholly lost` (JUST 2_500_000_000)) EQUALS 298_000_000
-- Provisions 1 and 3: not reinstated, or not yet incurred: Actual Value, 200,000,000 - 2,000,000.
#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`figures: reinstatement` 300_000_000 `, Actual Value` 200_000_000 `, reinstated and incurred` FALSE `, cost if wholly lost` (JUST 2_500_000_000)) EQUALS 198_000_000
-- Provision 2: a partial loss costs no more than a total one would (250,000,000 - 2,000,000).
#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`figures: reinstatement` 300_000_000 `, Actual Value` 280_000_000 `, reinstated and incurred` TRUE `, cost if wholly lost` (JUST 250_000_000)) EQUALS 248_000_000
-- Provision 2 needs that comparator; with none, the encoding refuses.
#ASSERT REFUSED `a house fire, settled on` (`figures: reinstatement` 300_000_000 `, Actual Value` 200_000_000 `, reinstated and incurred` TRUE `, cost if wholly lost` NOTHING) BECAUSE "Provision 2 needs the cost of reinstatement had the property been wholly lost"
-- A destroyed sofa needs no Provision 2 comparator: 40,000,000 - 2,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part 1: the amount payable, under` `the owner's policy` `with` `good conduct` `for` (`A Part 1 loss` WITH `the item claimed` IS `the Contents`, `the property` IS (LIST `furniture, a refrigerator, washing machine or similar household good`), `whose property` IS `the Insured`, `where the property was` IS `inside a lockable part of the Home`, `the date of the loss` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `the cause` IS `fire`, `the circumstances` IS EMPTY, `the extent` IS `lost or destroyed`, `sudden and unforeseen` IS TRUE, `consecutive days the Home had been left unattended` IS 0) `on` (`figures: reinstatement` 40_000_000 `, Actual Value` 25_000_000 `, reinstated and incurred` TRUE `, cost if wholly lost` NOTHING) `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS 38_000_000
-- Not covered: nothing is payable (an excluded fire, 1(a)).
#ASSERT `Part 1: the amount payable, under` `the owner's policy` `with` `good conduct` `for` (`a house fire with` `fermentation, natural heating or spontaneous combustion`) `on` (`figures: reinstatement` 300_000_000 `, Actual Value` 200_000_000 `, reinstated and incurred` TRUE `, cost if wholly lost` (JUST 2_500_000_000)) `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS 0

§§ `Settlement: limits, GC6, Pairs and Sets, GC9, Deductible`

-- The sum insured caps it (General Limit (a)): 2,000,000,000 - 2,000,000.
#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`figures: reinstatement` 2_600_000_000 `, Actual Value` 2_400_000_000 `, reinstated and incurred` TRUE `, cost if wholly lost` (JUST 2_600_000_000)) EQUALS 1_998_000_000

-- General Limit (b): 1,900,000,000 already paid this Period leaves 100,000,000; reinstated
-- by agreement, the full sum insured is available again.
GIVEN `paid` IS A NUMBER
      `reinstated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The figures for a Part 1 loss`
`figures for 300,000,000 with` `paid` `already paid, sum insured reinstated` `reinstated` MEANS
    `The figures for a Part 1 loss` WITH
        `the cost of reinstatement`                                      IS 300_000_000
        `the Actual Value`                                               IS 200_000_000
        `reinstatement was begun and carried out with reasonable dispatch` IS TRUE
        `the cost of reinstatement has actually been incurred`           IS TRUE
        `the cost of reinstatement had the property been wholly lost`    IS JUST 2_500_000_000
        `the cost had reinstatement been lawfully possible`              IS NOTHING
        `the pair or set`                                                IS NOTHING
        `the amount already paid on this item in the Period`             IS `paid`
        `the Insurer agreed to reinstate the sum insured`                IS `reinstated`
        `the sums insured by other insurances of the same loss`          IS EMPTY

#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`figures for 300,000,000 with` 1_900_000_000 `already paid, sum insured reinstated` FALSE) EQUALS 98_000_000
#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`figures for 300,000,000 with` 1_900_000_000 `already paid, sum insured reinstated` TRUE) EQUALS 298_000_000
#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`figures for 300,000,000 with` 2_000_000_000 `already paid, sum insured reinstated` FALSE) EQUALS 0

-- GC6: regulation prevents reinstatement; the lawful cost, 280,000,000, caps it.
#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`The figures for a Part 1 loss` WITH `the cost of reinstatement` IS 300_000_000, `the Actual Value` IS 290_000_000, `reinstatement was begun and carried out with reasonable dispatch` IS TRUE, `the cost of reinstatement has actually been incurred` IS TRUE, `the cost of reinstatement had the property been wholly lost` IS JUST 2_500_000_000, `the cost had reinstatement been lawfully possible` IS JUST 280_000_000, `the pair or set` IS NOTHING, `the amount already paid on this item in the Period` IS 0, `the Insurer agreed to reinstate the sum insured` IS FALSE, `the sums insured by other insurances of the same loss` IS EMPTY) EQUALS 278_000_000

-- GC9: another policy insures the same Home for 2,000,000,000 as well; the rateable share
-- of 300,000,000 is half, 150,000,000, less the Deductible.
#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`The figures for a Part 1 loss` WITH `the cost of reinstatement` IS 300_000_000, `the Actual Value` IS 290_000_000, `reinstatement was begun and carried out with reasonable dispatch` IS TRUE, `the cost of reinstatement has actually been incurred` IS TRUE, `the cost of reinstatement had the property been wholly lost` IS JUST 2_500_000_000, `the cost had reinstatement been lawfully possible` IS NOTHING, `the pair or set` IS NOTHING, `the amount already paid on this item in the Period` IS 0, `the Insurer agreed to reinstate the sum insured` IS FALSE, `the sums insured by other insurances of the same loss` IS (LIST 2_000_000_000)) EQUALS 148_000_000
#ASSERT `GC9: the rateable proportion of` 90 `, insured here for` 100 `and elsewhere for` (LIST 50, 50) EQUALS 45
#ASSERT `GC9: the rateable proportion of` 90 `, insured here for` 100 `and elsewhere for` EMPTY EQUALS 90

-- Pairs and Sets: one earring of a pair lost. Value of the part 12,000,000; the pair insured
-- for 20,000,000, so half is 10,000,000; reinstatement of the earring 15,000,000. Cap 10,000,000.
#ASSERT `Pairs and Sets: the cap on` 15_000_000 `for` (JUST (`A pair or set` WITH `the value of the parts lost, without special value as a pair or set` IS 12_000_000, `the number of parts lost or damaged` IS 1, `the number of parts in the pair or set` IS 2, `the sum insured on the pair or set` IS JUST 20_000_000)) EQUALS 10_000_000
-- Not separately insured: only the part's own value caps it.
#ASSERT `Pairs and Sets: the cap on` 15_000_000 `for` (JUST (`A pair or set` WITH `the value of the parts lost, without special value as a pair or set` IS 12_000_000, `the number of parts lost or damaged` IS 1, `the number of parts in the pair or set` IS 2, `the sum insured on the pair or set` IS NOTHING)) EQUALS 12_000_000
#ASSERT `Pairs and Sets: the cap on` 15_000_000 `for` NOTHING EQUALS 15_000_000

-- The Deductible comes off last and never below nothing: a 1,500,000 repair pays 0.
#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`figures: reinstatement` 1_500_000 `, Actual Value` 1_000_000 `, reinstated and incurred` TRUE `, cost if wholly lost` (JUST 2_500_000_000)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`figures: reinstatement` 2_000_000 `, Actual Value` 1_000_000 `, reinstated and incurred` TRUE `, cost if wholly lost` (JUST 2_500_000_000)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`figures: reinstatement` 2_000_001 `, Actual Value` 1_000_000 `, reinstated and incurred` TRUE `, cost if wholly lost` (JUST 2_500_000_000)) EQUALS 1

-- The layered scenario: covered, then Provisions (not reinstated: Actual Value 1,200,000,000
-- of a 2,600,000,000 cost), then General Limit (b) (1,000,000,000 already paid, so 1,000,000,000
-- remains), then GC9 (another 2,000,000,000 policy: half), then the Deductible:
-- min(1,200,000,000, 1,000,000,000) = 1,000,000,000; half = 500,000,000; less 2,000,000.
#ASSERT `a house fire, settled on` (`The figures for a Part 1 loss` WITH `the cost of reinstatement` IS 2_600_000_000, `the Actual Value` IS 1_200_000_000, `reinstatement was begun and carried out with reasonable dispatch` IS FALSE, `the cost of reinstatement has actually been incurred` IS FALSE, `the cost of reinstatement had the property been wholly lost` IS JUST 2_600_000_000, `the cost had reinstatement been lawfully possible` IS NOTHING, `the pair or set` IS NOTHING, `the amount already paid on this item in the Period` IS 1_000_000_000, `the Insurer agreed to reinstate the sum insured` IS FALSE, `the sums insured by other insurances of the same loss` IS (LIST 2_000_000_000)) EQUALS 498_000_000

§§ `Extensions 1-7 (src:343-404)`

#ASSERT `Extension 1: workmen doing repairs, minor alterations or decoration do not prejudice the policy`

-- Extension 2: the lesser of 40,000,000 and 5% of the item's sum insured, inclusive.
-- On 1,000,000,000 the 5% is 50,000,000, so 40,000,000 binds; on 600,000,000 the 5% is
-- 30,000,000, which binds.
#ASSERT `Extension 2: no inventory of undamaged property is needed for a claim of` 40_000_000 `on an item insured for` 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT NOT `Extension 2: no inventory of undamaged property is needed for a claim of` 40_000_001 `on an item insured for` 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `Extension 2: no inventory of undamaged property is needed for a claim of` 30_000_000 `on an item insured for` 600_000_000
#ASSERT NOT `Extension 2: no inventory of undamaged property is needed for a claim of` 30_000_001 `on an item insured for` 600_000_000
#ASSERT `Extension 2: no inventory of undamaged property is needed for a claim of` 40_000_000 `on an item insured for` 800_000_000
#ASSERT NOT `Extension 2: no inventory of undamaged property is needed for a claim of` 40_000_001 `on an item insured for` 800_000_000

GIVEN c1 IS A NUMBER
      c2 IS A NUMBER
      c3 IS A NUMBER
      c4 IS A NUMBER
      c5 IS A NUMBER
      c6 IS A NUMBER
      c7 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The costs claimed under the Part 1 Extensions`
`costs: fees` c1 `scale` c2 `fire fighting` c3 `debris` c4 `demolition` c5 `shoring` c6 `protection` c7 MEANS
    `The costs claimed under the Part 1 Extensions` WITH
        `the claim for this loss`                                   IS 0
        `architects', surveyors' and engineers' fees incurred`      IS c1
        `the fees allowed by the scales of the professional bodies` IS c2
        `fire fighting costs incurred`                              IS c3
        `costs of removing debris`                                  IS c4
        `costs of dismantling or demolishing`                       IS c5
        `costs of shoring or propping up`                           IS c6
        `costs of temporary protection`                             IS c7

-- Extension 3: the scale binds (120,000,000), or 10% of the Home's 2,000,000,000 (200,000,000).
#ASSERT `Extension 3: architects' and engineers' fees payable under` `the 2026 Summary` `on` (`costs: fees` 150_000_000 `scale` 120_000_000 `fire fighting` 0 `debris` 0 `demolition` 0 `shoring` 0 `protection` 0) EQUALS 120_000_000
#ASSERT `Extension 3: architects' and engineers' fees payable under` `the 2026 Summary` `on` (`costs: fees` 250_000_000 `scale` 230_000_000 `fire fighting` 0 `debris` 0 `demolition` 0 `shoring` 0 `protection` 0) EQUALS 200_000_000
-- Extensions 4 and 6: 10% of the Part 1 total of 2,500,000,000 is 250,000,000.
#ASSERT `Extension 4: fire fighting costs payable under` `the 2026 Summary` `on` (`costs: fees` 0 `scale` 0 `fire fighting` 300_000_000 `debris` 0 `demolition` 0 `shoring` 0 `protection` 0) EQUALS 250_000_000
#ASSERT `Extension 4: fire fighting costs payable under` `the 2026 Summary` `on` (`costs: fees` 0 `scale` 0 `fire fighting` 100_000_000 `debris` 0 `demolition` 0 `shoring` 0 `protection` 0) EQUALS 100_000_000
#ASSERT `Extension 6: temporary protection payable under` `the 2026 Summary` `on` (`costs: fees` 0 `scale` 0 `fire fighting` 0 `debris` 0 `demolition` 0 `shoring` 0 `protection` 260_000_000) EQUALS 250_000_000
-- Extension 5: the owner insures no Renovation Costs, so (b) and (c) are deleted: of
-- 30,000,000 debris + 50,000,000 demolition + 20,000,000 shoring only the 30,000,000 counts.
#ASSERT `Extension 5: limbs (b) and (c) are deleted under` `the 2026 Summary`
#ASSERT `Extension 5: debris removal payable under` `the 2026 Summary` `for` `the Home` `on` (`costs: fees` 0 `scale` 0 `fire fighting` 0 `debris` 30_000_000 `demolition` 50_000_000 `shoring` 20_000_000 `protection` 0) EQUALS 30_000_000
-- With all three items insured, all three count, capped at 10% of the item's sum insured.
#ASSERT NOT `Extension 5: limbs (b) and (c) are deleted under` (`The Policy Summary` WITH `the Period of Insurance begins` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `the Period of Insurance ends` IS YMD 2026 12 31, `the sum insured on the Home` IS JUST 2_000_000_000, `the sum insured on the Renovation Costs` IS JUST 100_000_000, `the sum insured on the Contents` IS JUST 500_000_000, `the Part 1 Limit of Liability` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for any one Occurrence` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for the Period` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 limit for food and drink` IS NOTHING, `the Part 1 Deductible` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 Deductible` IS NOTHING, `the Part 3 Deductible` IS NOTHING, `the Insured is named under Part 3` IS FALSE, `the domestic helper benefit is named` IS FALSE, `the construction of the Home is specially provided for` IS FALSE, `the annual premium` IS 0)
#ASSERT `Extension 5: debris removal payable under` (`The Policy Summary` WITH `the Period of Insurance begins` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `the Period of Insurance ends` IS YMD 2026 12 31, `the sum insured on the Home` IS JUST 2_000_000_000, `the sum insured on the Renovation Costs` IS JUST 100_000_000, `the sum insured on the Contents` IS JUST 500_000_000, `the Part 1 Limit of Liability` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for any one Occurrence` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for the Period` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 limit for food and drink` IS NOTHING, `the Part 1 Deductible` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 Deductible` IS NOTHING, `the Part 3 Deductible` IS NOTHING, `the Insured is named under Part 3` IS FALSE, `the domestic helper benefit is named` IS FALSE, `the construction of the Home is specially provided for` IS FALSE, `the annual premium` IS 0) `for` `the Contents` `on` (`costs: fees` 0 `scale` 0 `fire fighting` 0 `debris` 30_000_000 `demolition` 50_000_000 `shoring` 20_000_000 `protection` 0) EQUALS 50_000_000

-- A loss with its Extension costs, within the General Limit: a Home fire of 300,000,000,
-- fees 50,000,000 (scale 60,000,000), debris 30,000,000, fire fighting 10,000,000:
-- 300 + 50 + 30 + 10 = 390,000,000, less 2,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part 1: the amount payable with Extension costs, under` `the owner's policy` `with` `good conduct` `for` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `on` (`figures: reinstatement` 300_000_000 `, Actual Value` 200_000_000 `, reinstated and incurred` TRUE `, cost if wholly lost` (JUST 2_500_000_000)) `and` (`costs: fees` 50_000_000 `scale` 60_000_000 `fire fighting` 10_000_000 `debris` 30_000_000 `demolition` 0 `shoring` 0 `protection` 0) `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS 388_000_000
-- The same with the loss near the sum insured: the item's share stops at 2,000,000,000;
-- fire fighting (Part-wide) still adds 10,000,000: 2,010,000,000 less 2,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part 1: the amount payable with Extension costs, under` `the owner's policy` `with` `good conduct` `for` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `on` (`figures: reinstatement` 1_990_000_000 `, Actual Value` 1_500_000_000 `, reinstated and incurred` TRUE `, cost if wholly lost` (JUST 2_500_000_000)) `and` (`costs: fees` 50_000_000 `scale` 60_000_000 `fire fighting` 10_000_000 `debris` 30_000_000 `demolition` 0 `shoring` 0 `protection` 0) `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS 2_008_000_000

-- Extension 7: losses at hours 0, 10 and 72 are one event (the period 0-72, closed, F-72h);
-- 73 opens a second (73-145); 150 opens a third. So three Deductibles.
#ASSERT `Extension 7: the hours in one event` EQUALS 72
#ASSERT `Extension 7: the number of events, for losses at hours` (LIST 0, 10, 72, 73, 150) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Extension 7: the number of events, for losses at hours` (LIST 150, 73, 72, 10, 0) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Extension 7: the number of events, for losses at hours` (LIST 0, 72) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Extension 7: the number of events, for losses at hours` (LIST 0, 72.5) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Extension 7: the number of events, for losses at hours` EMPTY EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Extension 7: the Deductibles borne under` `the 2026 Summary` `for losses at hours` (LIST 0, 10, 72, 73, 150) EQUALS 6_000_000
#ASSERT `Extension 7 groups losses caused by` `flood`
#ASSERT NOT `Extension 7 groups losses caused by` `fire`
